# Changes to these files wait for a council member's review (council poll P35, 2026-11-10) once branch protection requires code owners' reviews
# (tools/ci/protect_pipeline.sh, docs/security.md). They are what builds, signs and ships releases, the code that
# checks downloads before installing them (backend.rs downloads, installs and updates the launcher itself; links.json
# says where from; the Cargo.toml files pick the crates that do it), and this file. Everything else merges as soon as
# `verify` passes.
/.github/                                @horizon-rust/council
/tools/ci/                               @horizon-rust/council
/tools/release_train.py                  @horizon-rust/council
/crates/horizon-release-sign/            @horizon-rust/council
/crates/horizon-server/src/update.rs     @horizon-rust/council
/crates/horizon-server/Cargo.toml        @horizon-rust/council
/launcher/src/signed.rs                  @horizon-rust/council
/launcher/src/backend.rs                 @horizon-rust/council
/launcher/links.json                     @horizon-rust/council
/launcher/Cargo.toml                     @horizon-rust/council
/packaging/                              @horizon-rust/council

# Two paths inside the folders above reach no secret, runner or release: the review of a Horizon Team member past probation is enough
# (#17630). The last matching line wins, so these stay below the folders. /nightly sets still refuse them
# (tools/ci/nightly_set.py).
/.github/pull_request_template.md        @horizon-rust/horizon-team @horizon-rust/council
/tools/ci/ignored-tests/                 @horizon-rust/horizon-team @horizon-rust/council
